Java Fibonacci Program Using Tabulation (DP)
import java.util.*;
class Main{
public static void main(String args[])
{
Scanner sc=new Scanner(System.in);
System.out.println("enter n value:");
int n=sc.nextInt();
int[] dp=new int[n+1];
dp[0]=0;
dp[1]=1;
for(int i=2;i<=n;i++)
{
dp[i]=dp[i-1]+dp[i-2];
}
System.out.println("the fibonacci value of n:"+n+"is"+dp[n]);
}
}
OUTPUT:
enter n value:
6
the fibonacci value of n:6is8
TIME COMPLEXITY:O(N)
SPACE COMPLEXITY:O(N)
    For Tabulation the optimized Space Complexity is O(1)
import java.util.*;
class Main{
public static void main(String args[])
{
Scanner sc=new Scanner(System.in);
System.out.println("enter n value:");
int n=sc.nextInt();
int prev2=0;
int prev1=1;
int current=0;
for(int i=2;i<=n;i++)
{
current=prev1+prev2;
prev2=prev1;
prev1=current;
}
System.out.println("the fibonacci number of n"+n+"is"+current);
}
}
